  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong, cohesive cyber-defense art direction: disciplined near-black palette, crisp cyan/pink accents, commanding headline, clear selected states, and thoughtful desktop-to-mobile restructuring. Below demo-ready polish because dense mono labels are extremely small and low-contrast, the desktop vector grid visibly clips content at the left edge, JSON content is awkwardly cropped, and the tablet/mobile header feels truncated rather than intentionally composed. Mobile’s long stacked card also loses hierarchy and becomes visually monotonous.",
    "fix": "Raise secondary-text contrast and minimum label size; eliminate clipping in the desktop grid and JSON panel; give the compact header a clearer active-location treatment; and strengthen mobile section separation with tighter spacing, bounded code overflow, and more deliberate detail-panel hierarchy.",
